-- title:
--   Cyclic cokernel for S-localisation of H²(G_{F,S},ℤ/p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $S$ be a finite set of rational primes with $p \in S$. Let $F$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` over $\mathbb{Q}$ which is Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$ and unramified outside $S$, i.e. $F/\mathbb{Q}$ is finite and for every prime $q \notin S$ and every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, the image in $\Gamma = \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ lies in $\Gamma_F =$ `F.fixingSubgroup`; assume moreover that if $p = 2$ then $F$ contains an element $i$ with $i^2 = -1$. For $q \in S$ write $K_q \le \Gamma$ for the range of the map $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q/\mathbb{Q}_q) \to \Gamma$ given by `extArithLoc S (Sum.inr q)`, and let $\gamma$ assign to each $q \in S$ and each coset $t \in \Gamma/(\Gamma_F \sqcup K_q)$ (the subgroup generated by $\Gamma_F$ and $K_q$) an element $\gamma_{q,t} \in \Gamma$ whose class is $t$. Put $D_{q,t} = \Gamma_F \cap \gamma_{q,t} K_q \gamma_{q,t}^{-1}$. Then there is a family $w_{q,t}$ of elements of `continuousH2` for the inclusion $D_{q,t} \hookrightarrow \Gamma$ with trivial $\mathbb{Z}/p$ coefficients (the quotient of the level $2$-cocycles by the level $2$-coboundaries lying in them) such that every family $y_{q,t}$ in these same modules can be written, for all $q$ and $t$, as $y_{q,t} = \operatorname{res}(x) + c\, w_{q,t}$, where $c \in \mathbb{Z}/p$ is a single scalar, $x$ is a single element of `continuousH2Sr` for $\Gamma_F \hookrightarrow \Gamma$, $S$ and trivial $\mathbb{Z}/p$ coefficients, and $\operatorname{res}$ denotes the image of $x$ under `continuousH2SrToContinuousH2` followed by `continuousH2Map` along the inclusion $D_{q,t} \le \Gamma_F$ with the identity on coefficients.
--
--   This is the existence half of degree-two Poitou–Tate global duality for the trivial module $\mathbb{Z}/p$ over an $S$-level Galois field $F$: the cokernel of the localisation map from the $S$-level $H^2$ of $\Gamma_F$ to the product of the local $H^2$'s at the places of $F$ above $S$ is generated by one element, the hypothesis $i \in F$ for $p = 2$ ensuring that the archimedean places contribute nothing. It is used by [`groupCohomology.exists_forall_locRes_continuousH2S_coind_trivial_eq_add_smul`](thm.html#groupCohomology.exists_forall_locRes_continuousH2S_coind_trivial_eq_add_smul), the corresponding statement for coinduced coefficients over $\mathbb{Q}$.
